  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing in-house consulting capacity for EU Member States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reforms to recalibrate the engagement of public administrations with private consulting services and to develop in-house consulting capacities are being initiated across the Member States. The project is designed to support such reforms in the public administrations of Austria, Belgium, Cyprus, the Czech Republic, France, Greece and Latvia. 

The request by the afore-mentioned Member States is funded by, and receives technical support from, the European Commission under Regulation (EU) 2021/240 establishing the Technical Support Instrument, with the Directorate-General for Structural Reform Support acting as the contracting authority and UNESCO as the implementing agency.</narrative>
  </description>
